    "['mep ccm-send mep-id [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm mep ccm send 3', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here is the translated Cisco equivalent command for `mep ccm-send mep-id 3 enable`:\\n\\n##\\nethernet cfm mep ccm send 3\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, the command to enable Continuity Check Messages (CCM) for a MEP (Maintenance End Point) uses the syntax `ethernet cfm mep ccm send <mep-id>`.\\n- The command enables CCM transmission for MEP ID 3, matching the functionality of the Huawei command.', 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm mep ccm send 3'}]]": 1,
