    "['remote-mep ccm-receive mep-id [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm mep ccm-receive 4 enable', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nethernet cfm mep ccm-receive 4 enable  \\n##  \\n\\nExplanation:  \\n- In Cisco, the equivalent command for enabling reception of Continuity Check Messages (CCM) from a remote MEP (Maintenance End Point) with ID 4 is `ethernet cfm mep ccm-receive <mep-id> enable`.  \\n- The syntax differs slightly from Huawei's `remote-mep ccm-receive mep-id <id> enable`, but the functionality is identical.  \\n- The command is placed under the CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) configuration mode in Cisco, similar to the Huawei context.\", 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm mep ccm-receive 4 enable'}]]": 1,
    "['test-id [parameter1] mep [parameter2] remote-mep [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm continuity-check mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for `test-id 1 mep 3 remote-mep 4`:\\n\\n##\\nethernet cfm continuity-check mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3\\nethernet cfm traceroute cache mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3\\n##\\n\\nNote: While Cisco's implementation of CFM (802.1ag) is similar in functionality, the exact command structure differs. The above commands:\\n1. Enable continuity check for the MEP\\n2. Configure traceroute caching for troubleshooting\\nThe test-id concept in Huawei maps to these maintenance operations in Cisco. Cisco doesn't have a direct 1:1 command for Huawei's test-id configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm continuity-check mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm traceroute cache mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for `test-id 1 mep 3 remote-mep 4`:\\n\\n##\\nethernet cfm continuity-check mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3\\nethernet cfm traceroute cache mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3\\n##\\n\\nNote: While Cisco's implementation of CFM (802.1ag) is similar in functionality, the exact command structure differs. The above commands:\\n1. Enable continuity check for the MEP\\n2. Configure traceroute caching for troubleshooting\\nThe test-id concept in Huawei maps to these maintenance operations in Cisco. Cisco doesn't have a direct 1:1 command for Huawei's test-id configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm traceroute cache mep mpid 3 vlan 2 domain md3 service ma3'}]]": 1,
